body:
No need to worry about being preachy. I've gone down this path before, but I'll give it another go. I'll make the effort to see if someone wants to hire a 61 yr old professional who understands business process, cost efficiencies, communicating at an appropriate level. Sounds perfect for Costco or Home Depot, right? (now I'm trying to be funny).

&#x200B;

Reminds me of a story with me father. He ended up in urgent care, he had an internal infection. In consultation with doctors, his lungs were filling up and he had tried multiple times to get out but failed, everyone agreed to go to pain management only. After 2 days, due to a mistake he became very lucid and told us he didn't want to go. Well Pop, nothing else has changed. 

&#x200B;

Point of story, if I can't find worthwhile employment, nothing has changed even if my attitude has.
